<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12764] Regression: Thin JDBC streaming fails/BatchUpdateException if function is used</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12764</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;insert INTO  city1(id,name,name1) VALUES(?,?,RANDOM_UUID())&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;happily worked in 2.7.6 but will fail on 2.8.0 with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.sql.BatchUpdateException: class org.apache.ignite.IgniteCheckedException: null&lt;br/&gt;
	at org.apache.ignite.internal.jdbc.thin.JdbcThinConnection$StreamState.readResponses(JdbcThinConnection.java:1364)&lt;br/&gt;
	at java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:834)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suspected reason is that function RANDOM_UUID() is not processed correctly here. Column type does not matter between UUID and VARCHAR.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
